 name: listing_source value outside whitelist is rejected (server-side whitelist)
 description: |
-  The `listing_source` <select> in `form_sections/work_income.gleam`
-  offers a fixed list (daft, myhome, facebook, word_of_mouth, other,
-  plus the empty "Select..." default). The server-side validator
-  `application_handler.is_valid_listing_source` mirrors that list and
-  the DB `application_listing_source_check` constraint enforces it at
-  the storage layer. A tampered DOM that injects an unknown value
-  (e.g. "blackhat-scraper") must be rejected with a `listing_source`
-  field error rather than landing in the database.
+  The form no longer renders the `listing_source` select (F4 field diet,
+  2026-08), but the server-side contract stands: the validator
+  `application_handler.is_valid_listing_source` and the DB
+  `application_listing_source_check` constraint still enforce the fixed
+  list (daft, myhome, facebook, word_of_mouth, other) for any posted
+  value — cached pages and raw clients can still send the field. A
+  hidden-input injection of an unknown value (e.g. "blackhat-scraper")
+  must be rejected with a `listing_source` field error rather than
+  landing in the database.
 
-  Mirrors `validation/invalid-guarantor-relationship` — the form's
-  fixed-list dropdowns get the same defense-in-depth pattern.
+  Was a `tamper_dropdowns` inject while the select existed; the
+  `tamper_hidden_inputs` hook tests the identical defended surface
+  without the rendered control.
